1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:48,840
EPISODE 10

7
00:00:56,682 --> 00:00:59,059
She said she suddenly
couldn't breathe properly.

8
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:00,978
That she's having trouble breathing.

9
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,604
Was she in a car accident?

10
00:01:02,688 --> 00:01:04,940
No, not a car accident.
It's just her breathing.

11
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,067
Please fill out
this registration form first.

12
00:01:09,361 --> 00:01:13,448
By any chance,
did she mention having any chest pain?

13
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,410
What kind of chest pain?

14
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:18,453
Like a stabbing pain
or something like that.

15
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:21,999
Ah.

16
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,458
-Excuse me for a second.
-Okay.

17
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,506
-I'm sorry. Just a second.
-Sure.

18
00:01:33,552 --> 00:01:34,553
Yes, hello?

19
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,055
Yeah, where are you now?

20
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:40,517
What?

21
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:25,520
Are you feeling better now?

22
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:30,651
How's your breathing?

23
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:35,697
Does your chest hurt
or feel tight or anything?

24
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:39,368
Yeah, I'm okay now.

25
00:02:40,369 --> 00:02:41,495
I feel better.

26
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:47,876
I was praying.

27
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:51,922
I said

28
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:56,093
I was thankful that Minjae's surgery
and chemo went well,

29
00:02:57,177 --> 00:02:58,929
and that he survived.

30
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:04,226
And I prayed he'd stay healthy,

31
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:07,604
just like he is now.

32
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:11,900
And then...

33
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:17,114
I prayed he'd meet someone better
than me, someone good for him,

34
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:20,742
and live a happy life with her.

35
00:03:25,122 --> 00:03:26,498
Is that all you prayed for?

36
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:31,378
You didn't pray
for Lee Jihoon's success or happiness?

37
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:34,881
No, I didn't.

38
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,342
That's stingy of you.

39
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:40,637
You're not even a Christian anyway.

40
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,306
Christian or not,
I believe in God. I pray, too.

41
00:03:44,182 --> 00:03:45,475
What about you?

42
00:03:45,559 --> 00:03:47,310
You're not a Christian either.

43
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,780
Please keep our Professor
Lee Jihoon healthy

44
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:01,491
and let everything he does go smoothly.

45
00:04:01,575 --> 00:04:03,952
Just let everything work out for him,
no matter what.

46
00:04:13,837 --> 00:04:18,091
Please keep Lim Youjin
healthy and happy, too.

47
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:24,473
I hope she'll never have
to suffer heartbreak or get hurt again.

48
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:26,641
And...

49
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:31,021
I pray that she'll smile a lot more
when she's with me.

50
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,105
Amen.

51
00:04:37,778 --> 00:04:38,862
Amen!

52
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:39,946
[chuckling] Gosh.

53
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:46,203
Right.

54
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:50,415
I didn't want to come empty-handed.

55
00:04:50,499 --> 00:04:52,417
Here's your Christmas present.

56
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,632
You said you got me something.

57
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:03,303
Hey, sorry. I left it at... home.

58
00:05:04,971 --> 00:05:05,972
Hmm.

59
00:05:06,264 --> 00:05:07,599
Did you buy this for me?

60
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:11,978
Hey, give me that.

61
00:05:12,062 --> 00:05:13,063
Oh, oh, oh.

62
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:19,986
Fine. It's a special occasion, so... here.

63
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:22,864
-What is it?
-Guess.

64
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:26,451
What is it? Is it expensive?

65
00:05:27,369 --> 00:05:29,329
Well, it's kind of expensive.

66
00:05:32,374 --> 00:05:33,542
It's yellow.

67
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:35,502
[in English] Yellow?

68
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:38,421
-Yellow?
-[in Korean] Yeah.

69
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:41,299
And it's sparkly.

70
00:05:42,259 --> 00:05:43,510
-Yellow and sparkly.
-Yeah.

71
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:46,346
[in English] Gold?

72
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:51,309
[in Korean] You know
how expensive gold is these days.

73
00:05:52,644 --> 00:05:53,645
Thank you.

74
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:55,272
Thanks.

75
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:00,318
I made them.

76
00:06:00,402 --> 00:06:01,570
Sparkly.

77
00:06:03,864 --> 00:06:04,865
Hmm.

78
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:08,910
It's not store-bought. It's handmade.

79
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:09,995
Yeah.

80
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:14,833
Didn't you have black yarn or anything?

81
00:06:15,417 --> 00:06:17,460
Hmm... There was no black yarn.

82
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:20,839
This was the only lambswool yarn
I had left at home.

83
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:22,090
You could've bought some.

84
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:24,968
I could have.
But I was too busy to go buy any.

85
00:06:26,177 --> 00:06:27,929
Aren't they cute, though?

86
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,975
And what did you get for me?

87
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:34,144
If it's not chocolate, what did you get?

88
00:06:38,398 --> 00:06:39,733
I didn't get you anything.

89
00:06:42,444 --> 00:06:45,113
I lied. I didn't get you anything.
So take these back.

90
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:51,745
I'm hungry.

91
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:53,163
Want to have some ramyeon?

92
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:05,819
-[staff] Welcome.

93
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,488
[woman] Dajeong! Over here.

94
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:17,956
Look at the shrimp and abalone.

95
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:20,959
It's good here, isn't it?

96
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:23,586
Yeah.

97
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,797
This is my secret spot,
so keep it to yourself.

98
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:33,179
What?

99
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:37,642
What do you think he was thinking?

100
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:39,936
Huh?

101
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:42,731
Because of me,

102
00:08:43,314 --> 00:08:44,941
because he didn't want me to worry,

103
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:48,403
he broke up with me
without even telling me he was sick.

104
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:49,946
Does that make any sense to you?

105
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:52,032
It just sounds like bullshit to me.

106
00:08:52,115 --> 00:08:54,200
-Right? It's bullshit.
-Yeah.

107
00:08:56,161 --> 00:08:57,912
And then he had the nerve to tell me...

108
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:01,124
He told me to let it all out,

109
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:03,543
and live happily ever after
with my husband.

110
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:04,961
That's bullshit too.

111
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:06,046
[Youjin] Yeah.

112
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:09,799
It's a little spicy.

113
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:11,468
Can I get a beer...

114
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,803
Me too.

115
00:09:16,181 --> 00:09:17,932
What do you want? Beer or highball?

116
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:19,059
Either one.

117
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:20,185
-[phone vibrating]
-Then beer.

118
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:29,944
Hello?

119
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:32,739
Hello?

120
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:36,367
<i>Hello?</i>

121
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:39,746
<i>Who are you? Say something.</i>

122
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:45,627
<i>I think you have the wrong number.</i>
<i>If you're not going to talk, I'll hang up.</i>

123
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,504
Hey, it's me.

124
00:09:48,213 --> 00:09:49,464
<i>It's Park Minjae.</i>

125
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:58,890
Well, I was wondering if you got home okay
or if something happened.

126
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:00,183
I was worried.

127
00:10:01,476 --> 00:10:02,936
[Jihoon] <i>Who's that? Who's calling?</i>

128
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:10,360
I can't really talk right now.
Next time...

129
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:12,946
I've got to go.

130
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,383
Thank you.

131
00:11:44,329 --> 00:11:45,330
Aren't you going in?

132
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:50,793
Aren't you going to go in?

133
00:11:54,756 --> 00:11:55,757
It's cold.

134
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:06,643
Why are you holding my hand
without asking?

135
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:07,810
Why not?

136
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:09,062
What's the big deal?

137
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:11,231
What's wrong with holding your hand?

138
00:12:11,314 --> 00:12:13,274
Your hand is so cold,
you can't feel a thing.

139
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,863
You barely had any beer,
and you're acting like a total drunk.

140
00:12:18,947 --> 00:12:20,782
I'm never going to drink with you again.

141
00:12:21,324 --> 00:12:23,243
I'm not acting like a drunk.
I'm not drunk.

142
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:24,327
Then what is it?

143
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,665
Is it because of Park Minjae?

144
00:12:31,668 --> 00:12:34,170
If you can't get over him
and you like him that much,

145
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:35,838
then get back together with him.

146
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:41,928
Don't you start crying here.

147
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,180
Don't you dare.

148
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:50,561
Do whatever you want.

149
00:12:57,902 --> 00:12:58,903
Give me those.

150
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,157
Give me those silly yellow gloves.
They're mine.

151
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:12,875
[muttering] What's wrong with him?

152
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:27,724
If I...

153
00:13:30,852 --> 00:13:32,645
If I asked you out, would you say yes?

154
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:35,732
What?

155
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:39,569
I did get you a gift.

156
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,529
A bracelet.

157
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:45,616
It's real gold,
not gold-plated or anything.

158
00:13:48,453 --> 00:13:49,579
Because it was pretty.

159
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:52,874
The second I saw it, I thought of you.

160
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:54,959
So I bought it without a second thought.

161
00:13:57,879 --> 00:13:59,672
If I give you that and ask you out,

162
00:14:01,841 --> 00:14:03,051
will you accept it?

163
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:09,432
What are you going to do?

164
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:13,519
What's your answer?

165
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:19,400
I'm not sure

166
00:14:21,152 --> 00:14:22,737
what you're talking about.

167
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,201
Fine.

168
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,287
You wait right here.

169
00:15:06,114 --> 00:15:07,698
MOM AND DAD ARE GOING TO HONGCHEON

170
00:15:07,782 --> 00:15:09,700
THERE'S CURRY IN THE POT, SO HELP YOURSELF

171
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:10,993
AND DON'T FIGHT, YOU TWO!

172
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:13,496
What does he even mean?

173
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,499
What am I supposed to do?

174
00:15:58,875 --> 00:16:02,712
LIM YOUJIN
MOBILE 010-0646-7905

175
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:25,109
Subin! Subin!

176
00:16:25,193 --> 00:16:27,612
-Subin! Here. Over here.
-Oh!

177
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:33,784
Sorry, I'm late.

178
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:37,079
No, you're not late at all.
The bus isn't even here.

179
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:38,372
Ah...

180
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:40,541
Oh, right.

181
00:16:44,962 --> 00:16:45,963
Merry Christmas.

182
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:49,717
Merry Christmas.

183
00:16:53,888 --> 00:16:55,014
Give me the bag.

184
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:57,099
What? No, I'm fine.

185
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:10,321
Oh.

186
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,865
Is that your snowboard?

187
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:15,743
Ah. Yes.

188
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:18,079
That's cool.

189
00:17:19,956 --> 00:17:22,458
Uh, it's not expensive or anything.

190
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:24,710
I just have one
because I like snowboarding.

191
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:27,088
It's cool.

192
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:29,465
This... It's not hard at all.

193
00:17:29,549 --> 00:17:31,676
You'll pick it up in no time.
I can teach you.

194
00:17:31,759 --> 00:17:32,760
Okay.

195
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:43,104
-Put this in your pocket.
-[chuckles]

196
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:44,772
Thank you.

197
00:17:50,945 --> 00:17:51,988
One second.

198
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:53,072
Okay.

199
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:56,534
Yes, hello?

200
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:57,618
Yes.

201
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:02,540
Yes.

202
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:06,252
Minjae!

203
00:18:07,962 --> 00:18:09,088
Have you been well?

204
00:18:10,965 --> 00:18:13,801
Yeah. Me too.

205
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,598
Well, I've been busy.

206
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:20,099
Just frantic.

207
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:21,642
Yeah.

208
00:18:21,726 --> 00:18:22,727
Okay.

209
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:25,813
Yeah.

210
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:28,941
Of course. Yeah.

211
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:39,994
Tomorrow?

212
00:18:43,748 --> 00:18:44,749
You're busy?

213
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:50,004
If you're busy, don't worry about it.

214
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:51,088
Yeah.

215
00:18:51,172 --> 00:18:52,965
Okay, then let's meet up with everyone.

216
00:18:53,049 --> 00:18:54,717
We can just meet all together. Yeah.

217
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,136
Okay.

218
00:18:58,262 --> 00:18:59,263
-Sejin.
-Yeah.

219
00:18:59,347 --> 00:19:00,431
The bus is here.

220
00:19:02,767 --> 00:19:03,976
All right.

221
00:19:14,195 --> 00:19:15,488
This is the bus, right?

222
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:32,213
Should we put it in here?

223
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:35,091
Yeah.

224
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:49,063
Here's the ticket.

225
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:56,737
-Um...
-Oh?

226
00:19:58,406 --> 00:20:00,032
-Subin.
-Yes?

227
00:20:00,116 --> 00:20:01,492
I'll take this one with me.

228
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:06,205
Uh...

229
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:11,377
I'm afraid...

230
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:17,758
I won't be able to go with you today.

231
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:20,261
What?

232
00:20:23,556 --> 00:20:24,682
I'm sorry.

233
00:20:38,529 --> 00:20:41,449
Call me when you get there.

234
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:47,848
Hey.

235
00:21:49,934 --> 00:21:51,852
It's been a while. Right?

236
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:54,605
-Minjae.
-[chuckles]

237
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:56,857
Oh, man. Okay.

238
00:21:58,776 --> 00:21:59,777
Let's go.

239
00:22:02,196 --> 00:22:04,573
Come on. Stop.

240
00:22:04,657 --> 00:22:05,699
[straining] Let go.

241
00:22:06,242 --> 00:22:07,701
I said let go, you freaking...

242
00:22:10,287 --> 00:22:11,288
You.

243
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:14,250
Hey, it's been so long. Right?

244
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:16,168
How long has it been?

245
00:22:16,252 --> 00:22:18,629
I'm sorry I haven't been in touch.

246
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,465
I heard you were sick.

247
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:24,301
How did you know?

248
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:26,804
I overheard Professor Ahn on the phone.

249
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:29,014
Oh.

250
00:22:29,974 --> 00:22:31,433
Are you all better now?

251
00:22:32,726 --> 00:22:35,646
I'm fine. The surgery went well.

252
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:36,730
I'm fine.

253
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:41,068
How about you? How have you been?

254
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:44,488
Well, I was just... I was doing fine.

255
00:22:44,572 --> 00:22:46,657
Going to school, studying...

256
00:22:48,576 --> 00:22:49,743
How about a girlfriend?

257
00:22:52,663 --> 00:22:56,542
You said you liked that,
you know, Jung Subin girl.

258
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:58,961
You said she was beautiful, like an angel.

259
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:01,171
Are you guys still in the talking stage?

260
00:23:01,255 --> 00:23:04,425
We're not in any stage.
We're just friends. She's a female friend.

261
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:06,218
Friends? You've got to be kidding me.

262
00:23:06,302 --> 00:23:08,596
Hey, after all the support I'd given you,

263
00:23:08,679 --> 00:23:11,432
there should've been
some progress, some results.

264
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:13,309
No, there's really nothing.

265
00:23:19,607 --> 00:23:22,318
How about Youjin? Is she doing well?

266
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:25,404
Well...

267
00:23:25,487 --> 00:23:29,158
I heard she was getting married soon.

268
00:23:29,783 --> 00:23:30,993
[yelling] She's getting married?

269
00:23:34,413 --> 00:23:35,497
She's not?

270
00:23:35,998 --> 00:23:37,207
Was I mistaken?

271
00:23:38,834 --> 00:23:39,835
Well,

272
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:42,046
not quite marriage.

273
00:23:43,631 --> 00:23:44,840
But she's seeing someone.

274
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:47,134
Oh.

275
00:23:47,593 --> 00:23:49,428
You know Professor Lee Jihoon from math?

276
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:51,096
I heard they're seeing each other.

277
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,557
But marriage...

278
00:23:53,641 --> 00:23:55,476
I don't think they're quite there yet.

279
00:23:56,727 --> 00:24:00,356
Well, if they keep seeing each other,
they'll eventually get married.

280
00:24:01,774 --> 00:24:05,569
But Professor Lee Jihoon
is an alpha, you know.

281
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:07,571
Alpha?

282
00:24:07,655 --> 00:24:10,908
I mean, he has a strong personality.
He's assertive and kind of prickly.

283
00:24:13,494 --> 00:24:17,206
Yeah. He's not exactly
the easiest person to deal with.

284
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:21,085
But apparently, he's popular with girls.

285
00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:22,920
They say he's sexy.

286
00:24:24,463 --> 00:24:25,756
He's sexy?

287
00:24:26,507 --> 00:24:28,425
What's so sexy about him?

288
00:24:28,509 --> 00:24:29,510
I'm not sure.

289
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:34,807
Women are attracted
to intellectual and smart men, you know.

290
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,558
Maybe it's that kind of sexiness?

291
00:24:39,436 --> 00:24:42,398
I'm like that myself,
so I kind of get the appeal.

292
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:44,400
Ah.

293
00:24:44,483 --> 00:24:45,693
That's right.

294
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:49,071
Yeah, he is sexy.

295
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:51,615
I can see why women feel that way.

296
00:24:55,494 --> 00:25:01,208
Anyway, people like him
have high standards for others too.

297
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:05,045
Honestly, I don't get how Lim Youjin
meets his standards...

298
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:08,924
She's not even that pretty,
and she has a weird personality.

299
00:25:09,008 --> 00:25:12,261
She's also dumb and stubborn.
There's nothing appealing about her.

300
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:16,974
Honestly, I don't even get
why you dated her.

301
00:25:17,057 --> 00:25:18,475
It's all over now, though.

302
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:25,607
Have you...

303
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:29,778
told anyone about me
and Youjin dating, by any chance?

304
00:25:29,862 --> 00:25:30,863
What?

305
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:33,490
No. I didn't tell anyone.

306
00:25:33,574 --> 00:25:35,951
Why would I talk about that?
It's your personal life.

307
00:25:38,871 --> 00:25:41,248
[sighs] But why...

308
00:25:42,499 --> 00:25:44,418
And talking about that

309
00:25:44,501 --> 00:25:47,087
would put Lim Youjin
in an awkward position.

310
00:25:47,838 --> 00:25:50,883
Who would want a woman with a past?

311
00:25:51,675 --> 00:25:52,885
A past?

312
00:25:52,968 --> 00:25:55,054
How is Youjin a woman with a past?

313
00:25:55,137 --> 00:26:00,059
Well, men don't want to know
about their girlfriend's exes, you know.

314
00:26:00,142 --> 00:26:02,102
It's kind of off-putting, to be honest.

315
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:06,190
Even just hearing about it
feels bad enough.

316
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:07,900
But seeing the guy in front of you?

317
00:26:07,983 --> 00:26:09,610
[sighs] That'd be seriously annoying.

318
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:14,448
You start hounding her,
getting suspicious, keeping tabs on her.

319
00:26:14,531 --> 00:26:16,408
Then you start suspecting she's cheating.

320
00:26:17,493 --> 00:26:19,286
Come on, that's what a psycho would do.

321
00:26:19,369 --> 00:26:22,164
Minjae, there are so many psychos
in this country.

322
00:26:23,832 --> 00:26:26,752
[sighs] There are nutjobs everywhere.

323
00:26:33,008 --> 00:26:36,386
Is that why he suggested
the three of us meet up?

324
00:26:37,054 --> 00:26:38,055
What?

325
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:42,518
So, he invited me to see how I'd react.

326
00:26:44,645 --> 00:26:46,814
Wow, what a psycho.

327
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:08,270
-Hey.
-Hello.

328
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:12,649
Have a seat.

329
00:28:16,945 --> 00:28:18,614
Hey, can you drink? You have cancer.

330
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:20,490
Oh...

331
00:28:21,491 --> 00:28:23,368
Well. Suit yourself.

332
00:28:23,452 --> 00:28:24,912
Can I get another glass, please?

333
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:26,538
Sure thing.

334
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:29,458
So, what is it you wanted to tell me?

335
00:28:31,376 --> 00:28:33,170
You said it was important.

336
00:28:36,632 --> 00:28:37,633
[staff] Here.

337
00:28:38,592 --> 00:28:39,718
-Thank you.
-[staff] Enjoy.

338
00:28:42,012 --> 00:28:43,388
Whatever it is, shoot.

339
00:28:52,564 --> 00:28:54,524
I'd like to know
your intentions, Professor.

340
00:28:55,067 --> 00:28:56,068
What intentions?

341
00:28:58,070 --> 00:29:00,572
That day, why did you suddenly...

342
00:29:00,656 --> 00:29:02,950
Wait, that thing on your face.

343
00:29:03,033 --> 00:29:05,077
On the right side. Is that a dimple?

344
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,161
Pardon?

345
00:29:06,787 --> 00:29:08,705
[Jihoon] When you smile.
Yeah, there it is.

346
00:29:08,789 --> 00:29:10,666
-This...
-Is it a dimple, not a wrinkle?

347
00:29:11,458 --> 00:29:12,542
Yes.

348
00:29:14,461 --> 00:29:16,046
I have dimples too.

349
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:24,513
It's not like you're insanely
good-looking or anything.

350
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:27,391
Definitely not something
you can't get over.

351
00:29:29,851 --> 00:29:31,728
I heard you told Youjin

352
00:29:31,812 --> 00:29:33,522
to get over you

353
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:35,607
and move on to someone better.

354
00:29:39,152 --> 00:29:41,905
She's trying so hard to move on
and build a happy life.

355
00:29:41,989 --> 00:29:44,408
Why did you come back?
What are you still hung up on?

356
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:48,370
I think there's a misunderstanding here.

357
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:52,541
Why? Is it hard to accept that things
between you two ended just like that?

358
00:29:53,125 --> 00:29:55,585
You just can't seem to move on?

359
00:29:57,004 --> 00:29:59,715
I'm not back because I haven't moved on.

360
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:02,509
I mean, you're the one
who broke up with her.

361
00:30:02,592 --> 00:30:03,719
Right?

362
00:30:03,802 --> 00:30:05,053
So just fuck off.

363
00:30:06,555 --> 00:30:09,850
It's true that I'm the one
who broke up with her.

364
00:30:09,933 --> 00:30:13,478
But if you just tell me to fuck off
without knowing the situation,

365
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:16,189
I've got a few things to say too...

366
00:30:18,483 --> 00:30:20,902
Situation, my ass. That's just bullshit.

367
00:30:20,986 --> 00:30:22,904
Want me to say
what you're really thinking?

368
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,992
What was I really thinking?

369
00:30:27,075 --> 00:30:28,368
You were confident.

370
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:32,956
The moment you broke up
with her, and even now.

371
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:36,001
Confident... What am I confident about?

372
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:39,671
You think you can go back
to how things were.

373
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:46,261
Honestly, a loser like you? I thought...

374
00:30:48,013 --> 00:30:49,514
Yeah.

375
00:30:49,598 --> 00:30:51,308
I definitely underestimated you.

376
00:30:53,727 --> 00:30:55,312
But it only took you five minutes.

377
00:30:57,397 --> 00:30:59,524
Man, you didn't even have to see her.

378
00:30:59,608 --> 00:31:02,569
One phone call with you,
and she just crumbled.

379
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:06,531
You arrogant,

380
00:31:07,616 --> 00:31:08,909
proud,

381
00:31:09,659 --> 00:31:10,911
entitled asshole.

382
00:31:14,748 --> 00:31:16,208
But it's not going to happen.

383
00:31:17,667 --> 00:31:18,877
Because she has me.

384
00:31:20,670 --> 00:31:23,131
It won't happen. It's too late.

385
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:27,844
What if I had died?

386
00:31:29,346 --> 00:31:31,223
What if I had died?

387
00:31:34,893 --> 00:31:36,645
Think about it.

388
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:39,648
If I had died,
what would that have done to her?

389
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:45,821
It was better to hurt her a little now
than hurt her even more later. Am I wrong?

390
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:50,575
This...

391
00:31:50,659 --> 00:31:52,661
This is unfair to me too. I...

392
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:54,371
It's not fair to me.

393
00:31:58,708 --> 00:32:00,919
You're a real piece of work, aren't you?

394
00:32:02,504 --> 00:32:05,215
Hey, are any of us gods here?

395
00:32:06,133 --> 00:32:07,676
Aren't we all just human?

396
00:32:08,677 --> 00:32:11,221
Fuck all that bullshit.
You like someone, you date them.

397
00:32:11,304 --> 00:32:14,057
It doesn't work out,
you break up. That's it.

398
00:32:14,141 --> 00:32:16,476
It's as simple as that.
How are you the victim here?

399
00:32:19,271 --> 00:32:20,272
Whatever.

400
00:32:20,939 --> 00:32:22,566
You had your chance, and it's over.

401
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:25,610
So stop playing with Youjin's feelings.

402
00:32:29,865 --> 00:32:31,074
You know what?

403
00:32:32,868 --> 00:32:34,995
You never know
what life might throw at us.

404
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:39,457
Watch out for cars. There are a lot
of car accidents out there.

405
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,086
Stay alive.

406
00:35:37,302 --> 00:35:40,472
[Miyoung] That's a lot of sesame seeds.

407
00:35:41,306 --> 00:35:43,350
It's not sesame seeds, it's sesame oil.

408
00:35:43,433 --> 00:35:46,186
Yeah, this is it.
Authentic sesame oil made in Korea.

409
00:35:46,269 --> 00:35:48,146
Was there a lot of snow in Hongcheon?

410
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:50,482
[groans] Tons of snow.

411
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:53,693
And with holiday traffic,
the roads were so backed up. It was awful.

412
00:35:53,777 --> 00:35:54,903
-Mom.
-Yeah?

413
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:57,113
Didn't Grandma ask why I didn't come?

414
00:35:57,197 --> 00:35:59,824
She did. She said she wanted to see you.

415
00:36:00,659 --> 00:36:04,329
That was it? Didn't she tell you
to give me some money or anything?

416
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:07,123
[Miyoung] Jeez, you should be the one
giving her money.

417
00:36:07,207 --> 00:36:08,625
[Youjin] I know. So immature.

418
00:36:08,708 --> 00:36:10,710
-[Miyoung sighs, groans]
-[Youjin grunts]

419
00:36:10,794 --> 00:36:11,878
Youjin,

420
00:36:12,379 --> 00:36:15,423
you know your great-aunt
in Hongcheon, right?

421
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:18,176
That great-aunt's
sister-in-law's father-in-law...

422
00:36:18,259 --> 00:36:20,053
No, that's not it.

423
00:36:20,136 --> 00:36:23,014
The sister-in-law's
husband's older brother.

424
00:36:23,098 --> 00:36:25,141
Honey, what does that make him to us?

425
00:36:25,767 --> 00:36:30,605
Wouldn't that make him
our in-law's in-law? No?

426
00:36:30,689 --> 00:36:31,690
I don't know.

427
00:36:31,773 --> 00:36:37,028
Anyway, that in-law's in-law is super rich
and owns a bunch of buildings.

428
00:36:37,112 --> 00:36:39,280
One of the buildings
is an assemblyman's office,

429
00:36:39,364 --> 00:36:41,700
so they're pretty close
with the assemblyman too.

430
00:36:41,783 --> 00:36:44,619
Apparently, that assemblyman's son
is your alum.

431
00:36:45,161 --> 00:36:46,913
He studied economics at Seohan.

432
00:36:47,872 --> 00:36:49,082
And he's 32.

433
00:36:49,165 --> 00:36:51,835
He's a Deputy Director at the MOFE.
What do you think?

434
00:36:52,961 --> 00:36:54,212
What do you mean?

435
00:36:54,754 --> 00:36:57,841
He's still just a civil servant.
That's not exactly a great catch.

436
00:36:58,883 --> 00:37:01,386
A Deputy Director is a Grade 5 official.

437
00:37:01,469 --> 00:37:03,972
He's not just any government worker.
He's a bureaucrat.

438
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:05,932
Right. He's a high-ranking bureaucrat.

439
00:37:06,015 --> 00:37:09,060
But if he's a politician's son
and a high-ranking bureaucrat,

440
00:37:09,144 --> 00:37:11,104
he must have plenty
of good matches. Why us?

441
00:37:11,730 --> 00:37:13,732
He's picky.

442
00:37:13,815 --> 00:37:16,401
No school bullying
in the past, no tax issues.

443
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:19,529
And most importantly,
he wants someone pretty.

444
00:37:19,612 --> 00:37:21,072
He says she can't be ugly.

445
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:23,658
-And that's her?
-Hey.

446
00:37:23,742 --> 00:37:25,702
You should show him her bare face.

447
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:28,079
What do you say? Do you want to meet him?

448
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,998
No. I'm busy. I can't.

449
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:32,208
Come on. Just meet up with him once.

450
00:37:32,751 --> 00:37:33,752
No.

451
00:37:33,835 --> 00:37:35,378
I knew you'd say that.

452
00:37:36,171 --> 00:37:39,424
Then do you have any friends
you could introduce him to?

453
00:37:39,507 --> 00:37:41,718
He's a really good catch.

454
00:37:44,304 --> 00:37:45,472
Hmm...

455
00:37:46,222 --> 00:37:47,348
How about Subin?

456
00:37:48,308 --> 00:37:49,434
Well, Subin is pretty.

457
00:37:49,517 --> 00:37:52,061
She's kind and well-behaved.
She also went to Seohan.

458
00:37:52,937 --> 00:37:54,898
Well, I don't know about Subin.

459
00:37:54,981 --> 00:37:55,982
Why not?

460
00:37:57,692 --> 00:37:59,486
Well, to be honest,

461
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:03,990
I've always wanted her
to be our daughter-in-law.

462
00:38:04,657 --> 00:38:05,658
[Youjin] What?

463
00:38:05,742 --> 00:38:07,952
-What? Me?
-[Youjin laughing]

464
00:38:08,036 --> 00:38:09,662
No way.

465
00:38:13,500 --> 00:38:16,169
Come on. You're being ridiculous now.

466
00:38:18,421 --> 00:38:19,881
Yeah, I know.

467
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,549
I know it's ridiculous.

468
00:38:22,926 --> 00:38:24,594
Well, it's just wishful thinking.

469
00:38:27,847 --> 00:38:30,809
Well. If only Youseong had gone
to a university in Seoul,

470
00:38:30,892 --> 00:38:33,436
I would've done whatever it took
to make it work.

471
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:35,146
What?

472
00:38:35,230 --> 00:38:39,275
Well, Youseong could
always go to college later.

473
00:38:40,485 --> 00:38:43,154
He's got a good personality.

474
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:44,781
And he's good-looking too.

475
00:38:46,241 --> 00:38:48,785
Even if he has a good personality
and is good-looking,

476
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:50,745
his academic background isn't good enough.

477
00:38:51,371 --> 00:38:53,665
Her parents wouldn't like it.

478
00:38:53,748 --> 00:38:55,875
A good personality and good-looking? Who?

479
00:38:58,294 --> 00:39:00,088
His background aside,

480
00:39:00,171 --> 00:39:03,049
Subin gets along with Youseong just fine.

481
00:39:04,634 --> 00:39:06,386
And they're close too.

482
00:39:06,886 --> 00:39:09,013
I mean, as long
as they like each other, right?

483
00:39:09,639 --> 00:39:12,016
It just doesn't work
like that in real life.

484
00:39:12,517 --> 00:39:13,768
Stop.

485
00:39:14,811 --> 00:39:18,189
Subin is just like a little sister to me.
I don't see her that way.

486
00:39:18,273 --> 00:39:19,357
She isn't even my type.

487
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:23,194
[sighs] That's enough.
You guys are just talking nonsense.

488
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:28,783
[Miyoung] Gosh.

489
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:34,163
This is why you should've
studied hard, like I told you to.

490
00:39:34,247 --> 00:39:35,373
Stop it.

491
00:39:35,456 --> 00:39:38,251
I said I'm not interested in Subin.
Why keep bringing it up?

492
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:42,755
Jeez.

493
00:40:35,683 --> 00:40:42,398
[automated voice]<i> The 650 bus</i>
<i>and the 5533 bus will be arriving shortly.</i>

494
00:40:44,567 --> 00:40:45,902
-Hey.
-Jesus Christ!

495
00:40:48,529 --> 00:40:49,530
Minjae!

496
00:40:51,491 --> 00:40:53,493
You haven't officially
started yet, have you?

497
00:40:53,618 --> 00:40:56,663
I still need to go clean things up
and get everything ready.

498
00:40:57,956 --> 00:41:00,708
Are you going
to be taking the shuttle bus to work?

499
00:41:00,792 --> 00:41:03,294
I think so. That's probably what I'll do.

500
00:41:04,587 --> 00:41:06,047
Aren't you going to buy a car?

501
00:41:06,130 --> 00:41:08,132
No, driving around
would be more of a hassle.

502
00:41:08,883 --> 00:41:10,969
But you're a professor.
You should have a car.

503
00:41:11,052 --> 00:41:12,929
I'm not a professor.

504
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:14,097
You are, though.

505
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:16,182
-It's here.
-It's here.

506
00:41:17,433 --> 00:41:18,726
Get in. Yeah, let's go.

507
00:41:18,810 --> 00:41:20,520
-It's a bit cold today.
-Yeah.

508
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:33,616
[Minjae] Hey, come on. Just sit there.

509
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:35,410
You always do this.

510
00:41:36,452 --> 00:41:38,037
-Subin.
-Hello.

511
00:41:38,121 --> 00:41:40,540
-It's been a while, right?
-[Subin] Yeah.

512
00:41:40,623 --> 00:41:42,333
Hello.

513
00:41:42,417 --> 00:41:44,460
-I heard you were back.
-Yeah.

514
00:42:14,699 --> 00:42:17,035
See you around, Subin. I'll keep in touch.

515
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:47,607
It's been so long
since I've been back on campus,

516
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:49,609
but it looks like it hasn't changed much.

517
00:42:49,692 --> 00:42:52,403
The buses, the roads, the field...

518
00:42:52,487 --> 00:42:54,363
Everything's just the same.

519
00:42:55,531 --> 00:42:57,158
And you haven't changed, either.

520
00:42:57,241 --> 00:43:00,453
You said you'd become a better person
by the time I got back.

521
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:02,830
You don't seem all that different to me.

522
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:10,338
Well, that's what you said then.

523
00:43:11,339 --> 00:43:13,257
Why are you bringing that up now?

524
00:43:14,383 --> 00:43:16,886
It's pointless and not funny.
What do you want?

525
00:43:19,013 --> 00:43:20,264
I mean...

526
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:22,975
We can't stay like this forever, you know.

527
00:43:28,231 --> 00:43:29,357
I messed up.

528
00:43:30,608 --> 00:43:32,735
I know I messed up too.

529
00:43:33,778 --> 00:43:34,779
So...

530
00:43:37,532 --> 00:43:38,866
Please forgive me.

531
00:43:40,409 --> 00:43:42,787
Okay, I forgive you.

532
00:43:43,871 --> 00:43:46,040
Now, be a better person,

533
00:43:46,124 --> 00:43:49,377
and when you meet someone new,
don't hurt her like you hurt me.

534
00:43:49,460 --> 00:43:51,671
I hope you find love
and happiness. All the best.

535
00:43:52,964 --> 00:43:54,257
[sighs] Uh, but...

536
00:43:55,049 --> 00:43:56,467
What are you two talking about?

537
00:43:58,136 --> 00:43:59,178
Nothing.

538
00:44:01,472 --> 00:44:02,557
Bye, Professor.

539
00:44:16,654 --> 00:44:19,657
PROFESSOR'S OFFICE

540
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:31,043
PARK MINJAE
PROFESSOR'S OFFICE

541
00:46:32,999 --> 00:46:34,667
[Jihoon] <i>What are you doing</i>
<i>after work today?</i>

542
00:46:40,798 --> 00:46:42,008
[Youjin] <i>Going home.</i>

543
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:47,054
[Jihoon] <i>Want to grab dinner together?</i>

544
00:46:57,189 --> 00:46:59,025
[Youjin] <i>Too tired.</i>
<i>Got to go home and sleep.</i>

545
00:47:52,870 --> 00:47:53,996
Where did everyone go?

546
00:47:54,914 --> 00:47:55,998
Oh.

547
00:47:56,082 --> 00:47:58,918
Professor Park Minjae's office.
They're having a meeting.

548
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:02,713
What? They should've told me about it.
Why didn't they say anything?

549
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:19,480
Aren't you going to the meeting?

550
00:48:21,357 --> 00:48:22,983
It's not a real meeting.

551
00:48:23,067 --> 00:48:25,611
They're just hanging out and chatting.

552
00:48:28,280 --> 00:48:29,532
It's not a meeting.

553
00:48:31,492 --> 00:48:32,493
Hey,

554
00:48:33,035 --> 00:48:34,787
even so, this isn't right.

555
00:48:35,246 --> 00:48:37,039
We should all be chatting together.

556
00:48:37,123 --> 00:48:38,999
We're all in the same lab, aren't we?

557
00:48:39,750 --> 00:48:42,211
-Don't you know what teamwork is?
-[sighs]

558
00:48:42,294 --> 00:48:43,921
Since when is hanging out teamwork?

559
00:48:44,004 --> 00:48:45,673
When we hang out, we stick together.

560
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:47,967
We look out for each other. That's family.

561
00:48:51,720 --> 00:48:52,721
You see,

562
00:48:54,390 --> 00:48:56,142
I've always wanted to say this to you.

563
00:48:58,394 --> 00:49:01,522
Do you know how easy they go on you
because you're the only girl?

564
00:49:01,605 --> 00:49:04,233
Hey, have I ever asked them
to go easy on me?

565
00:49:04,316 --> 00:49:05,609
There you go again.

566
00:49:07,194 --> 00:49:09,155
The guys just accepted
that you're different

567
00:49:09,238 --> 00:49:11,031
and treated you with care and respect

568
00:49:11,115 --> 00:49:13,284
as their junior and colleague.
And you say what?

569
00:49:13,367 --> 00:49:15,369
"When did I ever ask them
to go easy on me?"

570
00:49:16,912 --> 00:49:18,122
Go ahead, argue with me.

571
00:49:18,205 --> 00:49:19,248
Am I wrong?

572
00:49:20,207 --> 00:49:21,709
Hey, that's not what it is.

573
00:49:21,792 --> 00:49:22,793
Then what is it?

574
00:49:26,422 --> 00:49:29,717
Well, obviously, I'm uncomfortable
around Professor Park Minjae.

575
00:49:34,430 --> 00:49:36,348
If you're uncomfortable,

576
00:49:37,016 --> 00:49:38,017
then sit up straight.

577
00:49:38,559 --> 00:49:39,560
What?

578
00:49:39,643 --> 00:49:41,020
You think he's comfortable?

579
00:49:41,103 --> 00:49:43,272
He's uncomfortable too, but he's trying.

580
00:49:44,231 --> 00:49:47,860
Or why don't you just... just come clean?

581
00:49:47,943 --> 00:49:50,404
Say, "We secretly dated and broke up,
so it's awkward."

582
00:49:50,488 --> 00:49:51,864
Why don't you just do that?

583
00:49:55,284 --> 00:49:57,161
If you can't,

584
00:49:57,244 --> 00:49:58,370
don't make it obvious.

585
00:49:59,371 --> 00:50:00,748
If you're uncomfortable,

586
00:50:01,832 --> 00:50:02,833
deal with it.

587
00:50:27,483 --> 00:50:28,484
Yes?

588
00:50:29,485 --> 00:50:30,528
Hey, come in.

589
00:50:31,153 --> 00:50:33,364
I heard we were having a meeting here.

590
00:50:33,447 --> 00:50:34,698
[Minjae] Yeah. Come in.

591
00:50:35,324 --> 00:50:38,035
[Taeho] We're throwing
a welcome-back party for Minjae today.

592
00:50:38,118 --> 00:50:39,537
What should we eat?

593
00:50:40,204 --> 00:50:41,455
[Sejin] Oh.

594
00:50:41,539 --> 00:50:43,916
So this meeting's about
what we're having for dinner?

595
00:50:43,999 --> 00:50:45,042
Exactly.

596
00:50:46,001 --> 00:50:47,503
What should we have?

597
00:50:47,586 --> 00:50:49,380
Maybe pork belly? Maybe not.

598
00:50:50,673 --> 00:50:54,385
How about beef instead of pork?
It's been a while.

599
00:50:54,468 --> 00:50:55,719
Beef sounds great.

600
00:50:55,803 --> 00:50:58,889
Sirloin, tenderloin,
skirt steak, brisket. Right?

601
00:51:00,516 --> 00:51:03,811
Minjae is paying,
so let's get beef short ribs.

602
00:51:04,353 --> 00:51:06,146
-[Minjae scoffs]
-Yeah, beef short ribs.

603
00:51:06,230 --> 00:51:07,815
Beef short ribs? As if.

604
00:51:07,898 --> 00:51:10,943
Sejin, let's go with whatever you want.
It's on me.

605
00:51:11,026 --> 00:51:13,737
Oh. Then I'd say...

606
00:51:15,406 --> 00:51:16,407
Yeah?

607
00:51:17,491 --> 00:51:19,034
Fried chicken.

608
00:51:19,118 --> 00:51:20,619
Fried chicken sounds great.

609
00:51:20,703 --> 00:51:23,038
That's my junior.
Those guys are all strangers.

610
00:51:23,122 --> 00:51:25,416
You're the only one
I consider my brother. Thanks.

611
00:51:25,499 --> 00:51:27,585
All right, let's go with fried chicken.

612
00:51:27,668 --> 00:51:29,003
-Sejin, give me a hand?
-Sure.

613
00:51:29,086 --> 00:51:30,087
Yeah. All right.

614
00:51:31,630 --> 00:51:32,756
I'd love a draft beer.

615
00:51:37,803 --> 00:51:39,722
Did you book a table at the chicken place?

616
00:51:39,805 --> 00:51:42,224
Yeah, at Lulu Chicken, for six people.

617
00:51:42,308 --> 00:51:44,143
I wanted to have some beef.

618
00:51:45,978 --> 00:51:48,397
[Youjin] Oh? Are we going home already?

619
00:51:49,023 --> 00:51:51,150
No, not going home.
We're having a team dinner.

620
00:51:51,233 --> 00:51:53,027
We're throwing the welcome-back party
for Minjae today.

621
00:51:54,028 --> 00:51:55,029
Why?

622
00:51:55,946 --> 00:51:57,698
[Youjin] But I already have plans tonight.

623
00:51:59,533 --> 00:52:00,534
Really?

624
00:52:02,161 --> 00:52:04,538
What plans? Can't you cancel them?

625
00:52:04,622 --> 00:52:07,291
It's Minjae's welcome-back party.
It'd be nice if you came.

626
00:52:07,374 --> 00:52:10,502
Yeah, join us.
It's Minjae's first team dinner back.

627
00:52:11,420 --> 00:52:14,089
It's okay. If she can't make it,
she can't make it.

628
00:52:14,173 --> 00:52:15,966
Yeah. It's okay. Don't worry about it.

629
00:52:17,259 --> 00:52:19,136
But, Youjin,

630
00:52:20,179 --> 00:52:22,348
just send Minjae a quick text, okay?

631
00:52:22,431 --> 00:52:25,684
Tell him you're sorry you missed his party
and you'll see him next time.

632
00:52:25,768 --> 00:52:26,852
-[Youjin] I will.
-[Taeho] Good.

633
00:52:27,936 --> 00:52:29,229
-Bye.
-Bye.

634
00:52:29,313 --> 00:52:30,564
-Bye.
-Yeah.

635
00:52:31,815 --> 00:52:33,400
-Bye, Youjin.
-Good luck.

636
00:52:48,040 --> 00:52:49,625
[sighs] Done.

637
00:53:08,435 --> 00:53:11,230
-[door lock activates]
-[phone vibrates]

638
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:18,320
[Youjin] <i>I don't think I can</i>
<i>join the welcome-back party today.</i>

639
00:53:18,404 --> 00:53:19,446
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

640
00:53:25,994 --> 00:53:28,247
[Youjin] <i>Welcome back.</i>

641
00:53:49,351 --> 00:53:51,687
[Minjae] <i>Okay. Thanks.</i>

642
00:53:51,770 --> 00:53:52,855
<i>I'll see you around.</i>

643
00:54:06,410 --> 00:54:07,870
-Hello.
-Hello.

644
00:54:07,953 --> 00:54:10,789
Hi, I have a reservation for two
under the name Lee Jihoon.

645
00:54:10,873 --> 00:54:13,375
All right. Let me show you to your table.

646
00:54:13,459 --> 00:54:14,460
Okay.

647
00:54:20,215 --> 00:54:21,425
Here's your table.

648
00:54:21,508 --> 00:54:22,509
Thanks.

649
00:54:23,886 --> 00:54:25,846
May I take your bag and coat?

650
00:54:25,929 --> 00:54:28,557
Uh... I'll keep my bag.
Just the coat, please.

651
00:54:28,682 --> 00:54:29,683
Of course. Got it.

652
00:54:29,767 --> 00:54:30,768
Thank you.

653
00:54:31,393 --> 00:54:32,561
-Thank you.
-No problem.

654
00:55:04,801 --> 00:55:05,928
All right. [clears throat]

655
00:55:06,011 --> 00:55:07,679
Now that we've all had a few bites...

656
00:55:09,348 --> 00:55:13,310
The pride of our lab and my soulmate!

657
00:55:14,561 --> 00:55:18,232
Let's welcome Professor Park Minjae
on his triumphant return.

658
00:55:18,315 --> 00:55:20,776
Now, a round of applause.

659
00:55:20,859 --> 00:55:22,110
Welcome back.

660
00:55:22,194 --> 00:55:23,195
Thanks.

661
00:55:24,321 --> 00:55:28,951
All right. Now, let's hear a few words
from Professor Park.

662
00:55:29,034 --> 00:55:31,203
But before that, um...

663
00:55:31,286 --> 00:55:34,289
since he's come back from the States,

664
00:55:34,373 --> 00:55:38,293
we'll have him give his speech in English,

665
00:55:39,503 --> 00:55:41,171
which he's more comfortable with.

666
00:55:41,255 --> 00:55:43,465
-Jeez.
-[in English] Here you are. [laughs]

667
00:55:44,174 --> 00:55:45,342
[Hangyeol in Korean] Let's hear it.

668
00:55:46,760 --> 00:55:47,844
[in English] Okay.

669
00:55:47,928 --> 00:55:49,263
Uh...

670
00:55:49,346 --> 00:55:51,056
Thank you, everyone.

671
00:55:51,848 --> 00:55:53,308
Uh...

672
00:55:53,392 --> 00:55:55,018
I love you. Okay.

673
00:55:55,102 --> 00:55:56,853
-[in Korean] Bravo. All right.
-Youjin.

674
00:55:56,937 --> 00:55:58,272
Hey, Youjin.

675
00:55:59,147 --> 00:56:00,148
Huh?

676
00:56:00,232 --> 00:56:02,818
-You had plans. How did you make it?
-You made it.

677
00:56:03,569 --> 00:56:05,153
I pushed my plans back a bit.

678
00:56:06,029 --> 00:56:08,407
It's Minjae's party.
I should at least stop by.

679
00:56:10,242 --> 00:56:14,246
Our Youjin is so polite, right?

680
00:56:14,329 --> 00:56:17,791
She knows how to show respect
to her seniors. [laughs]

681
00:56:17,874 --> 00:56:19,585
-Yeah.
-Eat up.

682
00:56:19,668 --> 00:56:21,962
-Excuse me. Could we...
-I'm sitting up straight now.

683
00:56:22,045 --> 00:56:23,046
[Chansoo] Huh?

684
00:56:23,630 --> 00:56:25,674
Could we get a small plate, please?

685
00:56:25,757 --> 00:56:28,385
Minjae, welcome back to Korea.

686
00:56:29,928 --> 00:56:30,929
Thanks.

687
00:56:49,323 --> 00:56:51,450
-Let me refill your glass.
-Yes, thank you.

688
00:57:08,592 --> 00:57:09,593
Youjin.

689
00:57:10,761 --> 00:57:12,638
Let me walk you to the bus stop.

690
00:57:12,721 --> 00:57:15,307
It's okay. I'm going to take a taxi
because it's late.

691
00:57:15,390 --> 00:57:17,100
A taxi? Then let me get one for you.

692
00:57:17,184 --> 00:57:19,394
No, I'm fine. I can do it.

693
00:57:19,478 --> 00:57:21,438
No, you're late because of me.

694
00:57:21,521 --> 00:57:22,773
Come on, follow me.

695
00:57:26,860 --> 00:57:28,737
Are you meeting Professor Lee Jihoon?

696
00:57:30,197 --> 00:57:31,198
Yes.

697
00:57:32,783 --> 00:57:34,785
Is he nice to you?

698
00:57:37,162 --> 00:57:38,664
Yeah, I guess.

699
00:57:41,041 --> 00:57:42,417
He seems like a nice guy.

700
00:57:44,294 --> 00:57:46,254
He is. And he's really smart.

701
00:57:46,963 --> 00:57:47,964
And sexy?

702
00:57:49,007 --> 00:57:50,008
What?

703
00:57:50,634 --> 00:57:52,344
Well, Kim Sejin said

704
00:57:52,427 --> 00:57:55,097
Professor Lee is popular
with girls because he's sexy.

705
00:57:55,639 --> 00:57:57,766
Oh... As if.

706
00:58:01,269 --> 00:58:05,107
He's so full of himself,
and he says such mean things.

707
00:58:06,358 --> 00:58:08,819
He said Professor Lee
is popular with girls?

708
00:58:08,902 --> 00:58:10,112
Yeah.

709
00:58:10,195 --> 00:58:13,031
But there must be something
you find attractive about him

710
00:58:13,115 --> 00:58:14,449
if you're dating him.

711
00:58:15,701 --> 00:58:16,702
What?

712
00:58:17,411 --> 00:58:19,830
Who said I was dating him?

713
00:58:21,331 --> 00:58:22,457
-Huh?
-What crazy asshole

714
00:58:22,541 --> 00:58:23,750
is going around saying that?

715
00:58:27,504 --> 00:58:29,673
So, it's not true?

716
00:58:30,924 --> 00:58:32,300
Don't be ridiculous.

717
00:58:38,807 --> 00:58:42,310
If you're not marrying him or seeing him,

718
00:58:45,021 --> 00:58:46,857
can we get back together?

719
00:58:49,025 --> 00:58:50,026
No.

720
00:58:51,445 --> 00:58:55,157
Even if I beg you to forgive me
and promise I'll never do it again?

721
00:58:57,367 --> 00:58:58,368
No.

722
00:59:01,413 --> 00:59:05,292
I'm not making excuses,
but I really was sick.

723
00:59:05,375 --> 00:59:08,003
Back then, I honestly thought I might die.

724
00:59:08,086 --> 00:59:11,131
You don't know because I never told you
what was going on...

725
00:59:11,214 --> 00:59:12,215
I know.

726
00:59:13,383 --> 00:59:15,552
It must've been so painful
and hard for you.

727
00:59:16,553 --> 00:59:18,513
You were probably so overwhelmed

728
00:59:18,597 --> 00:59:20,766
that you couldn't think
about anything else.

729
00:59:21,850 --> 00:59:24,186
You were sick.
How could you think of anyone else?

730
00:59:24,269 --> 00:59:26,188
No, that's not what it was like!

731
00:59:26,271 --> 00:59:27,647
Don't yell at me.

732
00:59:30,901 --> 00:59:33,862
Whether I was too much,
things were too hard, whatever the reason,

733
00:59:35,447 --> 00:59:36,448
you left me once.

734
00:59:36,531 --> 00:59:38,033
How do I know it won't happen again?

735
00:59:38,116 --> 00:59:40,327
[yelling] No, I said that's not it!

736
00:59:40,410 --> 00:59:42,496
[yelling] I told you not to yell at me!

737
00:59:46,124 --> 00:59:48,043
All right. I... Don't cry. Come here.

738
00:59:48,126 --> 00:59:49,961
That was my bad. I'm sorry. I...

739
00:59:51,379 --> 00:59:53,298
I'm sorry. Don't cry, okay?

740
01:00:07,187 --> 01:00:09,564
But can you try to understand me too?

741
01:00:11,066 --> 01:00:13,819
I'm a coward,
and I always overthink everything.

742
01:00:13,902 --> 01:00:16,321
I always imagine the worst.

743
01:00:18,532 --> 01:00:19,574
I really...

744
01:00:20,784 --> 01:00:23,328
I really thought
I was going to die back then.

745
01:00:24,246 --> 01:00:25,247
That's why...

746
01:00:27,707 --> 01:00:30,001
I didn't want to make things hard for you.

747
01:00:30,085 --> 01:00:32,212
That's why I wanted to let you go.

748
01:00:32,295 --> 01:00:34,381
I don't want to hear any of that bullshit.

749
01:00:35,507 --> 01:00:37,926
You think you were the only one
having a hard time?

750
01:00:38,009 --> 01:00:39,719
You think you were the only one?

751
01:00:41,346 --> 01:00:44,015
I almost died back then too. I did too.

752
01:00:44,933 --> 01:00:46,726
I thought I'd rather die

753
01:00:47,227 --> 01:00:48,728
than break up with you.

754
01:00:48,812 --> 01:00:50,438
That's what I thought!

755
01:00:52,023 --> 01:00:55,610
You didn't die, but I died back then!

756
01:00:58,280 --> 01:01:00,574
So how am I supposed to forgive you?

757
01:01:01,199 --> 01:01:04,035
How am I supposed to take you back? How?

758
01:01:13,795 --> 01:01:15,672
My answer is no, and that's final.

759
01:02:53,603 --> 01:02:57,524
BETWEEN STEPS

760
01:02:57,607 --> 01:03:01,069
[Youjin] <i>I don't want any weird rumors</i>
<i>to start about you because of me.</i>

761
01:03:01,152 --> 01:03:02,570
I already like someone.

762
01:03:02,654 --> 01:03:05,824
<i>I gave you my whole heart, my everything.</i>

763
01:03:05,907 --> 01:03:08,076
<i>But you betrayed it</i>
<i>and just threw it away.</i>

764
01:03:08,159 --> 01:03:10,578
[Minjae] <i>Being with you made me happy,</i>

765
01:03:10,662 --> 01:03:13,123
<i>but it also really scared me.</i>

766
01:03:14,499 --> 01:03:17,043
<i>I was scared that one day, it'd all end.</i>

767
01:03:18,003 --> 01:03:19,546
<i>And that I'd be abandoned.</i>

768
01:03:20,505 --> 01:03:22,674
<i>You loved me,</i>

769
01:03:22,757 --> 01:03:24,050
<i>but I didn't.</i>
